  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They held it clean from the start and never let Arizona close.",
    "what_this_means": "Buehler lasted only four innings, which means the bullpen had to cover five with a one-run lead. Rodriguez, Estrada, Morejon, and Miller combined for five scoreless innings with six strikeouts and zero walks. That is how you protect a margin this thin. The Padres got what they needed early. Two runs in the third. And then stopped attacking. Twelve hits and only five runs scored is efficient, not explosive. But it was enough because the arm work behind it held. Rengifo went 3-for-5, Merrill drove in a run. The offense did its job and got out of the way. This is a team that wins when it doesn't need to score eight. Just enough, and the bullpen doesn't blink.",
    "what_to_watch": "Ronel Blanco starts for Houston with a 7.36 ERA, but the Astros are still dangerous late. Ray's 1.29 ERA over his last four starts is the real matchup to watch.",
